<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Why Does Daniel Eat His Pencil Case?</title>
    <style>
        body {
            background-color: #87CEEB; /* Soft Sky Blue */
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            color: #2c3e50;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        .card {
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
            border-radius: 20px;
            padding: 40px;
            max-width: 600px;
            width: 100%;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
            text-align: center;
        }

        h1 {
            color: #1e3c72;
            font-size: 2.2rem;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .subtitle {
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            color: #555;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            font-style: italic;
        }

        .theory-box {
            background: #ffffff;
            border-left: 5px solid #007bb5;
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 15px 20px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            text-align: left;
            box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
        }

        .theory-box h3 {
            margin: 0 0 8px 0;
            color: #007bb5;
        }

        .theory-box p {
            margin: 0;
            line-height: 1.5;
            color: #444;
        }

        .footer-note {
            margin-top: 25px;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            color: #666;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="card">
        <h1>The Mystery of Daniel's Pencil Case</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">An ongoing scientific investigation into Daniel's questionable snack choices.</p>

        <div class="theory-box">
            <h3>Theory 1: High Fiber Diet</h3>
            <p>Zipper canvas and synthetic polymers provide a texture unlike any regular food. Daniel believes it contributes to a balanced stationery diet.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="theory-box">
            <h3>Theory 2: Classroom Stress Relief</h3>
            <p>When math gets too tough, chewing on a pencil case is cheaper than therapy and tastes better than homework.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="theory-box">
            <h3>Theory 3: He Left His Lunch at Home</h3>
            <p>Why buy cafeteria food when you have a perfectly good fabric pouch full of graphite and eraser shavings right in front of you?</p>
        </div>

        <p class="footer-note">If you see Daniel, please remind him that stationery is for writing, not snacking.</p>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
